    │ components, optimizing list   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ performance, implementing     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ animations, or working with   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ native modules. Triggers on   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ tasks involving React         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Native, Expo, mobile          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ performance, or native        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ platform APIs.                │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 verification-before-completion           │ Use when about to claim work  │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ is complete, fixed, or        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ passing, before committing    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ or creating PRs - requires    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ running verification          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ commands and confirming       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ output before making any      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ success claims; evidence      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ before assertions always      │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 verify-implementation                    │ 프로젝트의 모든 verify        │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ 스킬을 순차 실행하여 통합     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ 검증 보고서를 생성합니다.     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ 기능 구현 후, PR 전, 코드     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ 리뷰 시 사용.                 │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 web-artifacts-builder                    │ Suite of tools for creating   │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ elaborate, multi-component    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ claude.ai HTML artifacts      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ using modern frontend web     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ technologies (React,          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui).     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Use for complex artifacts     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ requiring state management,   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ routing, or shadcn/ui         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ components - not for simple   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ single-file HTML/JSX          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ artifacts.                    │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 web-design-guidelines                    │ Review UI code for Web        │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ Interface Guidelines          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ compliance. Use when asked    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ to \"review my UI\", \"check     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ accessibility\", \"audit        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ design\", \"review UX\", or      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ \"check my site against best   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ practices\".                   │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 webapp-testing                           │ Toolkit for interacting with  │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ and testing local web         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ applications using            │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Playwright. Supports          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ verifying frontend            │                        │\n│               │                                             │ functionality, debugging UI   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ behavior, capturing browser   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ screenshots, and viewing      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ browser logs.                 │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 writing-plans                            │ Use when you have a spec or   │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ requirements for a multi-     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ step task, before touching    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ code                          │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 writing-skills                           │ Use when creating new         │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ skills, editing existing      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ skills, or verifying skills   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ work before deployment        │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 xlsx                                     │ Use this skill any time a     │ agents-skills-personal │\n│               │                                             │ spreadsheet file is the       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ primary input or output.      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ This means any task where     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ the user wants to: open,      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ read, edit, or fix an         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ existing .xlsx, .xlsm, .csv,  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ or .tsv file (e.g., adding    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ columns, computing formulas,  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ formatting, charting,         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ cleaning messy data); create  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ a new spreadsheet from        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ scratch or from other data    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ sources; or convert between   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ tabular file formats.         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Trigger especially when the   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ user references a             │                        │\n│               │                                             │ spreadsheet file by name or   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ path — even casually (like    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ \"the xlsx in my downloads\")   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ — and wants something done    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ to it or produced from it.    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Also trigger for cleaning or  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ restructuring messy tabular   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ data files (malformed rows,   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ misplaced headers, junk       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ data) into proper             │                        │\n│               │                                             │ spreadsheets. The             │                        │\n│               │                                             │ deliverable must be a         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ spreadsheet file. Do NOT      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ trigger when the primary      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ deliverable is a Word         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ document, HTML report,        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ standalone Python script,     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ database pipeline, or Google  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Sheets API integration, even  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ if tabular data is involved.  │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 ontology                                 │ Typed knowledge graph for     │ openclaw-workspace     │\n│               │                                             │ structured agent memory and   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ composable skills. Use when   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ creating/querying entities    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ (Person, Project, Task,       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Event, Document), linking     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ related objects, enforcing    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ constraints, planning multi-  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ step actions as graph         │                        │\n│               │                                             │ transformations, or when      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ skills need to share state.   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Trigger on \"remember\", \"what  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ do I know about\", \"link X to  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Y\", \"show dependencies\",      │                        │\n│               │                                             │ entity CRUD, or cross-skill   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ data access.                  │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 proactive-agent                          │ Transform AI agents from      │ openclaw-workspace     │\n│               │                                             │ task-followers into           │                        │\n│               │                                             │ proactive partners that       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ anticipate needs and          │                        │\n│               │                                             │ continuously improve. Now     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ with WAL Protocol, Working    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Buffer, Autonomous Crons,     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ and battle-tested patterns.   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ Part of the Hal Stack 🦞      │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 self-improvement                         │ Captures learnings, errors,   │ openclaw-workspace     │\n│               │                                             │ and corrections to enable     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ continuous improvement. Use   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ when: (1) A command or        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ operation fails               │                        │\n│               │                                             │ unexpectedly, (2) User        │                        │\n│               │                                             │ corrects Claude ('No, that's  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ wrong...', 'Actually...'),    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ (3) User requests a           │                        │\n│               │                                             │ capability that doesn't       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ exist, (4) An external API    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ or tool fails, (5) Claude     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ realizes its knowledge is     │                        │\n│               │                                             │ outdated or incorrect, (6) A  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ better approach is            │                        │\n│               │                                             │ discovered for a recurring    │                        │\n│               │                                             │ task. Also review learnings   │                        │\n│               │                                             │ before major tasks.           │                        │\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 tavily                                   │ AI-optimized web search via   │ openclaw-workspace     │\n│               │                                             │ Tavily API. Returns concise,  │                        │\n│               │                                             │ relevant results for AI       │                        │\n│               │                                             │ agents.                       │                        │\n└───────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────┘\n\nTip: use `openclaw skills search`, `openclaw skills install`, and `openclaw skills update` for ClawHub-backed skills.","cwd":"/home/lfant/.openclaw/workspace"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1774782988359}}
{"type":"message","id":"0b605e13","parentId":"ee1f7611","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:16:39.291Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"네, `self-improvement` 스킬이 이미 설치되어 있습니다.\n\n스킬 목록에서 다음과 같이 확인됩니다:\n\n```\n│ ✓ ready       │ 📦 self-improvement                         │ Captures learnings, errors,   │ openclaw-workspace     │\n```\n\n이 스킬은 다음과 같은 상황에서 자동으로 사용됩니다:\n- 명령이나 작업이 예기치 않게 실패할 때\n- 사용자가 Claude를 정정할 때 (\"No, that's wrong...\", \"Actually...\")\n- 사용자가 존재하지 않는 기능을 요청할 때\n- 외부 API나 도구가 실패할 때\n- Claude가 지식이 구식이거나 잘못되었다는 것을 깨달을 때\n- 반복 작업에 대해 더 나은 접근 방식이 발견되었을 때\n\n또한 주요 작업 전에 학습 내용을 검토합니다."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai","model":"glm-4.7","usage":{"input":15650,"output":227,"cacheRead":54617,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":70494,"cost":{"input":0.009389999999999999,"output":0.0004994,"cacheRead":0.00600787,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.015897269999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774782988376,"responseId":"202603291916329496c8af9fbd4522"}}
